Lower Bound + Parity Pattern

Core Idea

Sort → find first element >= x → use remaining count.

int low = 0, high = n - 1, ans = n;
while (low <= high) {
    int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;
    if (a[mid] >= x) {
        ans = mid;
        high = mid - 1;   // first occurrence
    } else {
        low = mid + 1;
    }
}

Recognition Trigger

* Array can be sorted
* Need first element >= x
* Multiple queries
* Result depends on elements after that position

Pattern

res = lower_bound(x)

* a[res] == x → special case
* Otherwise → count = n - res
* count % 2 == 0 → POSITIVE
* count % 2 != 0 → NEGATIVE

Complexity

Sort: O(n log n)
Each query: O(log n)
Total: O(n log n + q log n)
Space: O(1) extra

Memory Trick

Sort → Lower Bound → Check exact → Count remaining → Parity decides.
